														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4169472">
									

<p>The Keter reclassification was made before the Foundation realized what happened at Site 92. Instead of death of 4106, they thought it was a containment breach (the Foundation was in a very poor state that communication between sites is barely possible) and since Dr. Tsai, the only person 4106 isn't hostile towards can't contain it, containing 4106 would be a lot more difficult.</p>
<p>Of course they can just duct tape 4106 in its cage, but containing unimportant anomalies was not something the Foundation had the freedom to do after Protocol HOLOTHUROIDEA. Hence the Keter: Containing it would take a lot of effort and the Foundation won't do it anyway.</p>
<p>It wasn't tagged as Keter because it's considered neutralized judging from the note at the end of the article.</p>

